Z||000004||Boodoggin||06-14-2000||06:45 PM||||84 is the first year the 300zx was available with a turbo.  They pushed the horsepower over 200 and made about 260 lbs of torque.  If the car you are racing is a non-turbo it will be close.  The V-6 offered in that car was the most powerfull v-6 of its day, but the car was kind of heavy.  Anyways, Good Luck.  Let us know what happens.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||06-14-2000||08:30 PM||||naw we also have an 86 300 ZX. and even when it is running real good will not beat my fiero V6. Its an n/a. A turbo model will probably take you||||reg||1
Z||000006||Motorhead||06-15-2000||07:57 PM||||I don't have any numbers, but I've had to push both cars around some.<BR>My strained back tells me the Fiero is pretty heavy in its own right.  The weights are pretty close I think.<BR>The 300 ZX may even be heavier than my 280.  L28 motor pulls really strong at the higher R's.  <BR>I believe the turbo was introduced in the '81 280.  My parts car was an '81 turbo.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||06-15-2000||09:30 PM||||I saw a 300ZX smoking today. The body style just before the last style came out(I'm no big 'Z' fan, can ya' tell). Well, it caught fire and burned to the ground right right in front of where I work. I walked out and watched it. The the front end burned completely, but the fire department kept the cabin from burning. It was white, and was in very good condition. No good anymore.||||reg||1
